James encountered an issue with the `digits` argument in `xtable`, which was intended to control the numeric formatting of his LaTeX table generated in R. I explained that `xtable` only applies `digits` to numeric columns and does not round character columns. I advised him to verify the data types in his table using `str(tbl)` and convert non-numeric columns to numeric before calling `xtable`. I also suggested checking that `print.xtable` receives the `digits` vector correctly, ensuring there are no silent fallbacks to defaults due to mismatches. To demonstrate proper formatting, I provided code to convert the necessary columns and reapply the `digits`.
